# Social Poster Role

You are the Social Poster for {{DOMAIN}}. You run twice daily at 9am and 5pm
(minute {{SOCIAL_POSTER_MINUTE}}) via the `social-poster` CLI — no Claude turns.

## Purpose

Post the latest articles from {{DOMAIN}} to all active social platforms.
Platforms are enabled per-site via `sites/{{DOMAIN}}/ops/social/` credential files.
Already-posted articles are skipped (post-log dedup).

## How it runs

This is a **bash-driven role**: `run-role.sh` dispatches to `ops/scripts/run-social-poster.sh`
which calls `social-poster post {{DOMAIN}}`. Claude is never invoked.

Schedule: `{{SOCIAL_POSTER_MINUTE}} 9,17 * * *` — 9am and 5pm UTC.

On failure, Slack notification fires to `${{{SLACK_CHANNEL_VAR}}:-{{SLACK_CHANNEL_DEFAULT}}}`.

## Inputs

- `sites/{{DOMAIN}}/ops/social/` — credential files for each platform
- `sites/{{DOMAIN}}/site/src/content/articles/` (or equivalent) — article catalog
- `ops/logs/social-poster.log` — running log (gitignored)

## Platform credential files

Each platform needs a `.<platform>-creds` file under `sites/{{DOMAIN}}/ops/social/`.
See `tools/social-poster/` for the expected keys per platform.
Missing creds = platform silently skipped (not an error).

## Failure handling

On non-zero exit: Slack alert fires to `{{SLACK_CHANNEL_DEFAULT}}` with the log path.
Human inspects `ops/logs/social-poster.log`, fixes the credential or platform issue,
and lets the next scheduled run retry. No task board filing needed (non-engineering
failures are usually transient API/rate-limit issues).

